@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+-- Content Automation video styles (contract 1.2, additive; their integration request of 2026-10-08).
+--
+-- A course or a single video is now made in ONE of their styles — `character-arc` (the original
+-- illustrated Ali story, the default) or `motion-graphics` (flat motion graphics spoken to "you",
+-- built from named models and walk-throughs). The instructor picks it where they type the topic,
+-- and it is sent as `style` on plan, build and make-video.
+--
+-- WHY A COLUMN AND NOT ONLY `plan.style`. The plan is their shape and a single video has no plan
+-- at all; topic and series already live in columns because they are what WE asked for. The style
+-- is the same kind of fact, it is shown on the Library and status pages, and build reads it back
+-- before it charges anything.
+--
+-- NOT NULL DEFAULT 'character-arc': every row from before styles existed WAS made in that style,
+-- and their API reports exactly that for old items. A constant default is a metadata-only change
+-- on Postgres 11+, so this does not rewrite either table.
+--
+-- No CHECK constraint, on purpose — the same reasoning as `content_courses.status`: the set of
+-- styles is theirs and grows; the route validates against our list before a row is written.
+--
+-- FRESH-DATABASE SAFETY (Rule B). ALTER only, on tables the NUMBERED 0052 and 0054 create.
+-- Mirrored in migrate.ts.
+
+ALTER TABLE "content_video_jobs"
+  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS "style" text NOT NULL DEFAULT 'character-arc';
+
+ALTER TABLE "content_courses"
+  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS "style" text NOT NULL DEFAULT 'character-arc';
